yes, I do include supernatural merits here as &quot;regular&quot;). If we called Advanced Library &quot;Lore&quot; instead, and kept the same prerequisites, it wouldn't really change much. There's plenty of merits that chain off Safe Place - those are effectively Advanced Safe Place merits; Temple and the Wyrm Nest merits are pretty clear examples of that. Mother-Goddess' Alter is just Advanced Alter by another name. We have an Advanced merit that enhances the three Lashing Out merits. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, use those as a base, then make a third for an &quot;epic&quot; merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T06:36:39-07:00","id":1119487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1119373-ideas-for-advanced-and-epic-merits-for-vampires?p=1119438#post1119438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what about 10 dot merit that requires being an blood potency of 10 and a few other things that means no more toper</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this exist in a book or is it a suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:56:33-07:00","id":1119510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1119373-ideas-for-advanced-and-epic-merits-for-vampires?p=1119487#post1119487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this exist in a book or is it a suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only 10 dot merit I can imagine would be the most broken Mcguffing Artifact ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T08:27:35-07:00","id":1119520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1119373-ideas-for-advanced-and-epic-merits-for-vampires?p=1119510#post1119510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only 10 dot merit I can imagine would be the most broken Mcguffing Artifact ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have a similar reaction. I just wanted to be sure I hadn't missed something important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T08:33:15-07:00","id":1119523,"title":"","content":"There are Merits that can exceed five dots, but that's because you buy sub-Merits that adds to the dot total. No Merits has a fixed rating above five dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T11:05:09-07:00","id":1119574,"title":"","content":"There are 15 dot artifacts, in game.<br /> <br /> One of the 13 dot artifacts, the Metachronal Clock, is sort of a puzzlebox, but opening it allows you access to a private paradimension Place-That-Isn't that's been stocked with books.<br /> <br /> But as MCN pointed out, an Advanced or Epic Merit is a regular Merit that's been 'upgraded' and presumably is only available to supernaturals. The Beast book, which introduces them, for instance has Advanced and Epic Direction Sense, and Advanced Fast Reflexes.<br /> <br /> So for instance, Epic Automotive Genius might eliminate the modification limitation from your Crafting Skill altogether, allowing you to make any number of modifications to a vehicle, though individual modifications still have their limits intact, like the Durability modification capping out at +5.<br /> <br /> Thousand Years of Night has more vampire-relevant variants. They aren't explicitly called out as Epic or Advanced, but they don't really fit the description of them.<br /> <br /> Blood and Smoke has the Atrocious, Cutthroat and Enticing Merits which give you an 8-again quality on your invoking the respective Beast while Lashing Out or reacting to someone else Lashing Out.<br /> <br /> Thousand Years of Night, working off of having one of those as a prerequisite and needing you to be an Elder, has Undeniable Aura. 'Your character's Beast has become so powerful that his predatory aura spills out form him at all times. Anyone who remains in his presence for longer than a few minutes must reflexively roll Resolve + Blood Potency against your usual roll to lash out with the aspect of your character's Beast represented by the prerequisite Merit you possess. If you win, the first Social roll you make against that character in the current scene achieves an exceptional success on three dice instead of five.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T14:58:23-07:00","id":1119638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1119373-ideas-for-advanced-and-epic-merits-for-vampires?p=1119523#post1119523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Merits that can exceed five dots, but that's because you buy sub-Merits that adds to the dot total. No Merits has a fixed rating above five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 